<div xmlns:perseus="http://www.perseus.org/meta/perseus.rdfs#" xmlns:dctype="http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/" xmlns:tufts="http://www.tufts.edu/" xmlns:alph="http://alpheios.net/namespaces/tei" class="alpheios-lex-text_container en">
    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n104613" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">τρᾰχηλ-ίζω</span></b> , fut.
		
			Att.
		
		<div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>A.</b>
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">-ιῶ</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					<u>PPetr.</u>
					2p.52
				</span></i>
			
			<span class="entity">(iii B. C.)</span>:—<i>bend</i> or <i>twist the
				neck of</i> a victim, 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">βοῦν</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Thphr.
					<u>Char.</u>
					27.5
				</span></i>
			. </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense2"><b>II.</b> in
			wrestling, '<i>scrag</i>' one's opponent, 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">τοὺς νεανίσκους</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Plu.
					<u>Ant.</u>
					33
				</span></i>
			:— 
				Pass.
			, <i><span class="en">
				Pl.
				<u>Amat.</u>
				132c
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				Teles
				p.50
			</span></i> H., <i><span class="en">
				Them.
				<u>Or.</u>
				23.291b
			</span></i>. </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense3"><b>2.</b> metaph.,
				<i>inflict hardship on</i> a combatant, 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">τοὺς . . φίλους οἱ λειπόμενοι
					τραχηλιοῦσι πόλεμοι</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Ph.
					2.131
				</span></i>
			:—
				Pass.
			, 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἐμφυλίῳ πολέμῳ καὶ διχονοίᾳ
					-ιζόμενοι</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					J.
					<u>BJ</u>
					4.6.2
				</span></i>
			. </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense3"><b>3.</b> metaph. in 
				Pass.
			, <i>to be overpowered, swept away,</i>
			
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ταῖς ἐπιθυμίαις</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Ph.
					2.127
				</span></i>
			; of ships in a whirlpool, <i><span class="en">
				Str.
				6.2.3
			</span></i>. </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense2"><b>III.</b> in a pun
			on signfs. <i><span class="en">
				1
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				11.1
			</span></i>, and <i><span class="en">
				11.3
			</span></i>, <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἰδὼν Ὀλυμπιονίκην εἰς ἑταίραν
				πυκνότερον ἀτενίζοντα, "ἴδε" ἔφη, "κριὸν Ἀρειμάνιον
				ὡς ὑπὸ τοῦ τυχόντος κορασίου -ίζεται"</span> see how
			the ram's <i>neck is being twisted,</i>
			<i><span class="en">
				D.L.
				6.61
			</span></i>, cf. <i><span class="en">
				Plu.
				2.521b
			</span></i>; <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">τοὺς πολυπράγμονας ἴδοις ἂν
				ὑπὸ παντὸς ὁμοίως θεάματος -ιζομένους καὶ
			περιαγομένους</span> ibid. </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense2"><b>IV.</b>
			
				Pass.
			, <i>to be laid open,</i>
			<i><span class="en">
				Ep.Hebr.
				4.13
			</span></i>; <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">τετραχηλισμένα: πεφανερωμένα,</span>
			<i><span class="en">
				Hsch.
			</span></i></div>
    </div> <div class="alpheios-lex-footnotes en"> </div>
